---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { breadcrumbStructuredData, webPageStructuredData } from "../lib/seo";
import { absoluteSiteUrl, withBase } from "../lib/site";

const canonicalUrl = absoluteSiteUrl("/privacy/");
const description =
  "Reviewable privacy draft for the stark AI Developer skills-only package and its repository site.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  structuredData={[
    webPageStructuredData({ canonicalUrl, description, title: "Privacy" }),
    breadcrumbStructuredData([{ name: "Privacy", url: canonicalUrl }]),
  ]}
>
  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="hero-copy" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Reviewable draft · last reviewed 2026-08-18</p>
      <h1>Privacy boundary</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy__lead">
        stark AI Developer is a skills-only package. This page describes the intended
        package boundary and remains subject to legal and publisher review before public
        submission.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-panel" aria-labelledby="privacy-status">
      <h2 id="privacy-status">Draft status</h2>
      <p>
        This repository-local page is not legal advice, a completed privacy notice, or
        evidence of a verified public deployment.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="catalog-band prose" aria-labelledby="package-data-title">
    <h2 id="package-data-title">What the package does</h2>
    <p>
      The package provides Markdown skill instructions, OpenAI skill metadata, references,
      scripts, templates, and static assets. It does not operate a backend, MCP server,
      connector, account system, authentication flow, telemetry, analytics pipeline,
      hidden network call, or runtime download.
    </p>
    <h2>Data the package may encounter</h2>
    <p>
      When a host client uses a skill, the client or model may receive the prompt,
      repository files, workspace metadata, command output, diagrams, memories, or other
      artifacts that the user deliberately makes available. The package does not
      independently collect, retain, sell, profile, or transmit those categories.
    </p>
    <h2>What the package does not control</h2>
    <p>
      The host client, workspace, repository, installed tools, shell, browser, model
      provider, and any external service may process user content under their own policies.
      A skill cannot turn those host capabilities on and must not claim that it inspected,
      executed, rendered, uploaded, or mutated anything without evidence from the host.
    </p>
    <h2>Repository and site processing</h2>
    <p>
      The catalog site is built from repository files. GitHub Pages, GitHub, the skills
      installer, and the selected client may process requests or installation metadata
      independently of the package. Confirm the final hosting provider notice, analytics
      settings, contact, retention, controller, and cross-border terms during legal review.
    </p>
    <h2>v1 package privacy answers</h2>
    <p>
      These answers apply to the skills-only package. They are not a completed
      legal notice and do not describe processing by ChatGPT, Codex, GitHub,
      GitHub Pages, a selected host, workspace, repository, or third-party tool.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Categories of personal data collected by stark AI through the package:</strong>
        none. The package does not send prompts, repositories, files, outputs, or
        credentials to stark AI.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Purposes of processing by the package:</strong> none. The package
        does not independently collect, retain, sell, profile, or transmit user data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Categories of recipients from the package:</strong> none.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Retention periods for the package:</strong> none. The package does
        not store personal data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>User controls and contact:</strong> use the
        <a href={withBase("/support/")}>support draft</a> for repository questions
        and the <a href={withBase("/security/")}>security-report draft</a> for
        suspected vulnerabilities. Final privacy contact, jurisdiction, and
        data-subject process remain legal-review items.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Host and product processing:</strong> ChatGPT, Codex, the user's
        selected host, workspace, repository, installer, and tools may process
        content under their own policies. This package cannot guarantee those
        processors.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Accounts, backend, telemetry:</strong> v1 has no stark AI account,
        backend, telemetry, analytics, or hidden network calls.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Support and security reports:</strong> handled through the support
        and security-report drafts above. Those routes are not a live public
        intake until legal and publication review complete.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Site requests and retention</h2>
    <p>
      This catalog is a static site built from public repository files. The hosting provider,
      GitHub, browsers, client installers, and model providers may process HTTP requests,
      security logs, installation metadata, or content under their own notices. The
      repository does not set the provider's retention period, analytics configuration,
      controller, subprocessors, jurisdiction, or cross-border transfer terms; confirm
      those details during legal review.
    </p>
    <h2>External publication gates</h2>
    <p>
      A repository build cannot prove that these pages are live over HTTPS, that a publisher
      identity is verified, that Apps Management access is configured, or that a supported
      client completed add, enable, update, disable, and remove operations. Those are
      external review gates and remain pending until separately evidenced.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
